==Trivia==
*"Sugadinti" means "to ruin" <sup>''(verb)''</sup> or "ruined" <sup>''(adjective)''</sup> in Lithuanian.
*Upon release, the Maiden of Sugadinti was the tallest boss model when she performs her attack animation.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ghost|url=https://twitter.com/Jagex_Ghost/status/971092264855498752|date=6 March 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964016|archivedate=13 May 2026|quote=Today I've been working on The Maiden's animations and realised at one point she becomes our tallest OS boss model yet! [https://pbs.twimg.com/media/DXoDQd3X0AEc5_j.jpg]}}
*The Maiden's appearance is extremely similar to that of the [[Hespori]], a rare carnivorous plant from [[Morytania]]; it's been confirmed that there may be a link between the two.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1084257292709711872|date=13 January 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107461|archivedate=29 April 2020|quote=[The Hespori bears a striking resemblance to the Maiden from TOB. It's also a plant from Morytania. Is there a possible link between the two?] Yes :)}} This link is explored in detail during the quest [[A Night at the Theatre]], in which it is revealed that the Maiden was created using Hespori bark.{{CiteNPC|npc=Ranis Drakan|quote=When we created the Maiden, we experimented heavily in that area.}}{{CiteNPC|npc=Ranis Drakan|quote=Precisely that! Specifically the hespori. Their bark has wonderful regenerative abilities.}}
*The name "The Maiden of Sugadinti" was given to her by [[Verzik Vitur]], which [[Ranis Drakan]] found surprising.{{CiteNPC|npc=Ranis Drakan|quote=I must say, I find the name you've given her to be quite interesting. Not the kind of thing I'd have expected from you.}} Both Verzik and the [[Mysterious Stranger]] refer to the name choice as ironic.{{CiteNPC|npc=Verzik Vitur|quote=It seemed an ironically fitting role for her, given that fun little narrative you came up with. Besides, with all the work you put in, it would have felt wrong to just abandon her.}}{{CiteNPC|npc=Mysterious Stranger|quote=The Maiden of Sugadinti. Such an ironic name.}} During [[The Blood Moon Rises]], it is revealed that Sugadinti is the name of Verzik's father, whom she usurped after he refused to unite the Vitur clan with the Drakan clan.

